-- ============================================================
-- Fight Zone V1 — default public content (generated by
-- scripts/gen-default-content-sql.ts from lib/legal/templates.ts).
-- Publishes Privacy v1 / Terms v1 and the FAQ ONLY when none exist yet,
-- so it never overwrites anything Seif already wrote.
-- ============================================================

insert into public.legal_documents (kind, version, title, content, status, published_at)
select 'privacy', 1, 'Privacy Policy', $fz$Fight Zone ("we", "us") is the boxing, kickboxing and fitness coaching platform of Coach Seif Dridi in Tunisia. This policy explains what personal data the platform collects, why, who can see it and the rights you have. It applies to the website, the member area and the admin area.

## 1. Data controller
The data controller is Fight Zone, operated by Coach Seif Dridi. You can reach us at any time through the [Contact page](/contact).

We process personal data in line with Tunisian Organic Law n° 2004-63 of 27 July 2004 on the protection of personal data and, for visitors and members located in the European Union, with the principles of the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).

## 2. What we collect
- **Account data:** your name, email address and password. Passwords are never stored in readable form — only a secure hash managed by our authentication provider.
- **Profile data (optional):** phone number, date of birth, gender, address, skill level, weight, height, a short bio and a profile photo. You choose what to fill in.
- **Event data:** the events you register for, your registration status, the amount due, the payment method you plan to use, your payment status and the attendance recorded by Coach Seif.
- **Payment evidence:** if you pay by bank transfer, the receipt (image or PDF) you upload, the amount and reference you declare, and Coach Seif's decision. We never ask for card numbers, bank passwords or online-banking access, and the platform itself does not process any payment.
- **Messages:** your private conversation with Coach Seif, including photos and documents you send, and automatic Fight Zone notices about your registrations and payments.
- **Achievements:** badges earned from attended events and any rewards granted, used or withdrawn.
- **Contact form:** your name, email address, topic and message.
- **Technical data:** the cookies strictly needed to keep you signed in, and server logs (time, page, technical errors) used to keep the service secure and working.

## 3. Why we use it (purposes and legal bases)
| Purpose | Legal basis |
|---|---|
| Creating and running your account | Performance of our agreement with you |
| Managing event registrations, capacity, waitlists and attendance | Performance of our agreement with you |
| Reviewing manual payments and keeping payment records | Performance of the agreement and legal accounting obligations |
| Private messaging and automatic notices about your activity | Performance of the agreement |
| Badges and rewards based on attendance | Our legitimate interest in recognising participation |
| Answering contact requests | Your request / our legitimate interest |
| Security, fraud prevention and error monitoring | Our legitimate interest and legal obligations |

We do not sell your data, we do not use it for advertising, and we do not make automated decisions that have legal effects on you.

## 4. Who can see your data
- **You** — everything in your account.
- **Coach Seif** (the only administrator) — the information needed to run events: your profile, registrations, payment plans and evidence, attendance, achievements and your conversation with him.
- **Other members** never see your private profile, messages, payment evidence or registrations.
- **Technical service providers** that host or operate parts of the platform for us, under confidentiality and security obligations:
  - Supabase — database, authentication and file storage;
  - Netlify — website hosting;
  - Resend — transactional emails (for example event reminders);
  - Google (Gemini) and Groq — used only to generate a generic daily motivational quote. **No personal data is sent to them.**

Some of these providers process data outside Tunisia. Where this happens, we rely on their contractual and security safeguards, in line with the applicable rules on cross-border transfers.

## 5. Payment evidence and private files
Receipts and message attachments are stored in **private storage**. They can only be opened by you and Coach Seif, through secure links that expire after a short time. Uploading a receipt does **not** confirm a payment — only Coach Seif's review does.

Profile photos are stored as images reachable by a hard-to-guess link and are shown in your conversations with Coach Seif.

## 6. Cookies
We only use cookies that are strictly necessary for the platform to work (keeping you signed in and remembering basic preferences). We do not use advertising or tracking cookies, and no consent banner is therefore required for them.

## 7. How long we keep data
- **Account and profile:** while your account is active. If you ask us to delete your account, we delete or anonymise it, except what we must keep by law.
- **Registrations, payments and receipts:** kept with the related payment record for as long as accounting and tax law requires.
- **Messages:** while your account is active.
- **Contact-form messages:** as long as needed to answer you, then deleted periodically.
- **Server logs:** short-term, for security and troubleshooting.

## 8. Your rights
Under Tunisian law (and the GDPR where it applies) you have the right to:
- **access** your data and obtain a copy;
- **correct** inaccurate data — most of it directly from your profile;
- **delete** your data, or **object** to its use, when there is no legal reason for us to keep it;
- **restrict** processing, and, where applicable, **receive your data** in a portable format;
- **withdraw consent** at any time where processing is based on consent.

To exercise these rights, message Coach Seif from your account or use the [Contact page](/contact). We answer as quickly as possible and at the latest within the legal time limits. You may also lodge a complaint with the Tunisian personal data authority (**INPDP — Instance Nationale de Protection des Données Personnelles**) or, if you live in the EU, with your local data protection authority.

## 9. Security
We use encrypted connections (HTTPS), per-user access rules enforced by the database, private storage for sensitive files, short-lived access links and an audit trail of sensitive administrative actions. No system is perfectly secure; if a breach affecting your data occurs, we will inform you and the competent authority as required by law.

## 10. Minors
Members under 18 must have the permission of a parent or legal guardian, who is responsible for the information provided.

## 11. Changes
When we update this policy we publish a new version here, with its version number and date. Previous versions remain available at the bottom of this page.$fz$, 'PUBLISHED', now()
where not exists (select 1 from public.legal_documents where kind = 'privacy');

insert into public.legal_documents (kind, version, title, content, status, published_at)
select 'terms', 1, 'Terms of Use', $fz$These Terms of Use govern the Fight Zone platform, operated by Coach Seif Dridi in Tunisia. By creating an account or registering for an event, you accept them. Please read them together with our [Privacy Policy](/privacy).

## 1. The service
Fight Zone lets you discover boxing, kickboxing and fitness events, register for them, follow your registration and payment status, message Coach Seif and track your achievements. Events are organised and run by Coach Seif.

## 2. Your account
- You must provide accurate information and keep it up to date.
- Keep your password confidential; you are responsible for activity on your account. Tell us immediately if you think it has been misused.
- Members under 18 need the permission of a parent or legal guardian.
- We may suspend an account that breaks these terms or puts others at risk. You may stop using the platform and ask us to close your account at any time.

## 3. Events and registration
- Each event page shows its date, place, format, capacity, price (in Tunisian dinars, or free) and any requirements.
- **Places are limited.** A registration is confirmed only when its status shows *Confirmed*. Some events require Coach Seif's approval first.
- When an event is full, you may join its **waitlist** if available; places that free up are offered automatically in order of registration.
- **Private events** are visible only to invited members.
- You may register only yourself, once per event.
- Coach Seif may change or cancel an event (for example for safety, illness or force majeure). Registered members are notified in the platform.

## 4. Cancellations by members
You can cancel your registration from your account until the deadline shown on the event. After that deadline, or once your payment has been confirmed, please message Coach Seif. Repeated no-shows may lead to registration requests being declined.

## 5. Prices and payment
- **There is no online payment on Fight Zone.** You pay Coach Seif **in person** or by **bank transfer**.
- Before registering for a paid event you choose how you will pay. If you choose bank transfer, you indicate when you will make it, and you can upload your receipt once it is done.
- The amount due is fixed when you register: later price changes do not affect your registration.
- An uploaded receipt is only evidence. Your payment is confirmed **only when Coach Seif confirms it**. He may reject evidence that does not match (amount, reference, transfer not received), with a reason; you can then upload a new receipt or pay in person.
- **Refunds:** the platform does not process refunds. If an event is cancelled by Fight Zone, or in any other situation, any refund or credit is agreed directly with Coach Seif.

## 6. Badges and rewards
Badges are earned from attendance recorded by Coach Seif. Rewards, when offered, are personal, non-transferable, single-use, may expire, have no cash value, cannot be combined with other offers unless stated, and are subject to the terms shown with each reward. Fight Zone may correct badges or rewards awarded by mistake.

## 7. Health, safety and conduct
- Combat sports involve physical contact and a risk of injury. Take part only if you are fit to do so, tell Coach Seif about any medical condition or injury before training, and follow his instructions and the safety rules of each session.
- Respect other members, the coach and the venue. Violence outside supervised training, harassment, discrimination or abusive messages are not tolerated.
- Do not upload unlawful, offensive or misleading content, or other people's personal data without their permission.

## 8. Content and intellectual property
The Fight Zone name, logo, texts, photos and designs belong to Fight Zone or its licensors and may not be reused without permission. You keep ownership of what you upload, and allow Fight Zone to store and display it only to provide the service.

## 9. Availability and liability
We work to keep the platform available and secure but cannot guarantee uninterrupted service. To the extent permitted by Tunisian law, Fight Zone is not liable for indirect losses, or for damage caused by misuse of the platform, by failure to follow safety instructions, or by events beyond our reasonable control. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot legally be limited, including for gross negligence or intentional misconduct.

## 10. Personal data
We handle your data as described in our [Privacy Policy](/privacy), in line with Tunisian Organic Law n° 2004-63 and, where applicable, the GDPR.

## 11. Changes to these terms
We may update these terms. The new version is published here with its version number and date; continuing to use the platform after an update means you accept it. Previous versions remain available at the bottom of this page.

## 12. Governing law and disputes
These terms are governed by Tunisian law. In case of disagreement, please contact us first so we can find an amicable solution. Failing that, the competent Tunisian courts will have jurisdiction, without prejudice to any mandatory consumer protection rules that apply to you.

## 13. Contact
Questions about these terms: use the [Contact page](/contact) or message Coach Seif from your account.$fz$, 'PUBLISHED', now()
where not exists (select 1 from public.legal_documents where kind = 'terms');

insert into public.faq_items (category, question, answer, position, is_published)
select v.category, v.question, v.answer, v.position, v.is_published
from (values
      ($fz$General$fz$, $fz$What is Fight Zone?$fz$, $fz$Fight Zone is Coach Seif Dridi's boxing, kickboxing and fitness coaching platform. You can discover events, register, follow your payment, message Coach Seif and track your achievements — all in one place.$fz$, 1, true),
      ($fz$General$fz$, $fz$Do I need experience to join?$fz$, $fz$No. Each event shows its level and requirements. If you're unsure whether an event is right for you, message Coach Seif before registering.$fz$, 2, true),
      ($fz$General$fz$, $fz$Is creating an account free?$fz$, $fz$Yes. Creating an account is free and takes a minute. You only pay for paid events you register for.$fz$, 3, true),
      ($fz$Events$fz$, $fz$How do I register for an event?$fz$, $fz$Open the event, choose how you'll pay if it's a paid event, then press **Register**. Your status appears immediately on the event page and in **My events**.$fz$, 4, true),
      ($fz$Events$fz$, $fz$What does “Awaiting approval” mean?$fz$, $fz$Some events are confirmed by Coach Seif personally. Your place is held while he reviews your request, and you're notified as soon as he decides.$fz$, 5, true),
      ($fz$Events$fz$, $fz$The event is full — can I still join?$fz$, $fz$If the event has a waitlist, join it. When a place frees up, the oldest waitlisted member gets it automatically and is notified.$fz$, 6, true),
      ($fz$Events$fz$, $fz$Can I cancel my registration?$fz$, $fz$Yes, from the event page, until the cancellation deadline shown on the event. After the deadline — or once your payment is confirmed — message Coach Seif.$fz$, 7, true),
      ($fz$Events$fz$, $fz$What are private events?$fz$, $fz$Private events (for example one-to-one coaching) are visible only to the members Coach Seif invites.$fz$, 8, true),
      ($fz$Payments$fz$, $fz$How do I pay?$fz$, $fz$There is no online payment. You pay Coach Seif **in person** or by **bank transfer**. You choose your method before registering; the bank details are shown on the event page once you're registered.$fz$, 9, true),
      ($fz$Payments$fz$, $fz$I paid by bank transfer — what now?$fz$, $fz$Upload your receipt from the event page. Coach Seif checks that the money arrived and confirms your payment. Until then your status shows **Proof under review** — that is not yet a confirmation.$fz$, 10, true),
      ($fz$Payments$fz$, $fz$My receipt was rejected. What should I do?$fz$, $fz$The reason is shown on the event page and in your messages. Fix the issue and upload a new receipt, pay in person, or reply to Coach Seif in Messages.$fz$, 11, true),
      ($fz$Payments$fz$, $fz$Can I get a refund?$fz$, $fz$Refunds are not processed by the platform. If an event is cancelled or you can't attend, talk to Coach Seif directly in Messages.$fz$, 12, true),
      ($fz$Account$fz$, $fz$How do I contact Coach Seif?$fz$, $fz$Use **Messages** in your member area — it's your private conversation with him. Visitors without an account can use the [Contact page](/contact).$fz$, 13, true),
      ($fz$Account$fz$, $fz$How do badges and rewards work?$fz$, $fz$Every event Coach Seif records as attended counts toward milestone badges. Some badges unlock a reward (for example a discount), which Coach Seif applies to an eligible event. See **Achievements** in your member area.$fz$, 14, true),
      ($fz$Account$fz$, $fz$How can I update or delete my data?$fz$, $fz$Update your details in **Profile**. To access, export or delete your data, message Coach Seif or use the Contact page — see our [Privacy Policy](/privacy).$fz$, 15, true)
) as v(category, question, answer, position, is_published)
where not exists (select 1 from public.faq_items);
